Regression UI: derive/proc-macro expansions must NOT be flagged by
FULLY_QUALIFIED_PATH_WITHOUT_USE. clap's derive rewrites user-written
short type tokens (e.g. `String`) into absolute paths while KEEPING the
original token's span, so `from_expansion()` alone does not fire; the
syntax-context and snippet-segment-count guards catch this.

Expected warnings (fully_qualified_path_without_use) — none from the
derive bodies; only the hand-written fully qualified paths:

warning: fully qualified path `crate::util::helper` used instead of a `use` import
  --> src/lib.rs:39:5

warning: fully qualified path `std::mem::drop` used instead of a `use` import
  --> src/lib.rs:40:5

Requires `clap = { version = "4", features = ["derive"] }` to compile;
kept as a sample since dylint_testing is incompatible with the pinned
nightly.
